{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow","id":1172797,"title":"Path to Jerusalem CoW","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-02T16:28:16-08:00","id":1172797,"title":"Path to Jerusalem CoW","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So, I wanted some thoughts on a spell that was spoiled through Dave Brookshaw's awesomeness regarding the Signs of Sorcery Book. According to the information from the 2E Core here is the information regarding Focused Mage Sight and CoW:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the mage employs Scrutiny on a subject protected by some kind of magical concealment, the Storyteller should use the same metric as Active Mage Sight for determining whether a Clash of Will is appropriate. If a Clash of Wills is appropriate, the mage\u2019s player receives the rote quality on the roll. </div> </div> </div>And then there is the spell description as provided by the spoiler:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Path to Jerusalem (Prime \u2022\u2022) </b><br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Opacity<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Expression, Larceny, Subterfuge<br /> This spell, named for the labyrinth at the Cathedral of Chartres, has been variously used by mages attempting to conceal their involvement in illicit activities, frame their rivals, or simply stymie other occult investigators. Add the spell's Potency to the Opacity of the subject Mystery.<br /> +1 Reach: Every Reach spent allows the mage to plant one false piece of Surface or Deep Information in the Mystery, either concealing a true piece of information or adding an entirely new falsehood. This can include placing another mage's Signature Nimbus on the Mystery, if the caster has studied it. Recognizing the falsehood requires a Clash of Wills while examining the Mystery with Focused Mage Sight. </div> </div> </div>So, does the mage receive the rote quality on the CoW against a spell that's only purpose is to confuse mages using Focused Mage Sight? Or should it just receive the normal Gnosis + Arcanum vs. Gnosis + Arcanum. My gut feeling is that it is the normal CoW and not the rote quality boosted version referenced in the Focused Mage Sight, but I thought I would reach out to see what everyone else thought. My reasoning is also founded on the fact that the 2E Core references if a CoW would be provoked when using Active Mage Sight but that could also be tripped if someone was using it to analyze a spell that was concealing another effect entirely. Or perhaps it is a combination of the two in which it could be they get Rote Quality to bypass the initial aspect, but get the normal CoW when trying to bypass the Path to Jerusalem.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:38:45-08:00","id":1172799,"title":"","content":"Prime Sight would get rote factor on the clash, other Arcana wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T18:34:44-08:00","id":1172816,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks for the clarification. I plan on using that in my upcoming gaming session. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:44:20-08:00","id":1172860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172799#post1172799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime Sight would get rote factor on the clash, other Arcana wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please dont make the withstand something that the spell manipulates. It doesnt work. You add the spells potency to the withstand of the spell which then cant beat the withstand because they are the same. Opacity 3, spell potency 4 vs withstand 3 leaves potency 1, new withstand 4 vs spell potency 4, oh dear no more spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:56:06-08:00","id":1172864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172860#post1172860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please dont make the withstand something that the spell manipulates. It doesnt work. You add the spells potency to the withstand of the spell which then cant beat the withstand because they are the same. Opacity 3, spell potency 4 vs withstand 3 leaves potency 1, new withstand 4 vs spell potency 4, oh dear no more spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you coming up with that? Nothing in the spell implies it messes with Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:57:31-08:00","id":1172866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172864#post1172864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you coming up with that? Nothing in the spell implies it messes with Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Withstand: Opacity,<br /> <br /> What does the spell do? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Add the spell's Potency to the Opacity of the subject Mystery.</i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:59:10-08:00","id":1172867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please dont make the withstand something that the spell manipulates. It doesnt work. You add the spells potency to the withstand of the spell which then cant beat the withstand because they are the same. Opacity 3, spell potency 4 vs withstand 3 leaves potency 1, new withstand 4 vs spell potency 4, oh dear no more spell. </div> </div> </div>This was actually an argument raised in a previous thread, it was determined that a spell can't check its withstand against itself. What would happen, in terms of mechanics is you would have an Opacity that fluctuated constantly between 3 &amp; 4 as the spell reapplied &amp; no longer applied it's potency bonus to the Mystery's Opacity creating a quantum state of always on &amp; always off. However, this was not the design of magic to have it check its own Withstand. Because there is a Matter spell that has Durability as a Withstand and it increased Durability.<br /> <br /> There were also examples of lowering Resolve/Composure through Mental Spells and thus creating a chain effect that would reduce someone's Resolve/Composure down to 1, but again this is circular logic that was not intended, only if the Withstand changes outside the spell's mechanics do you re-evaluate Withstand. You can also use another spell to increase the Withstand against a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Spelling error. 01-03-2018, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:01:52-08:00","id":1172869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172866#post1172866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Withstand: Opacity,<br /> <br /> What does the spell do?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s to cast the spell in the first place, reducing Opacity via Scrutiny doesn\u2019t deal with Withstand at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:06:34-08:00","id":1172871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172867#post1172867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was actually an argument raised in a previous thread, it was determined that a spell can't check its withstand against itself. What would happen, in terms of mechanics is you would have an Opacity that fluctuated constantly between 3 &amp; 4 as the spell reapplied &amp; no longer applied it's potency bonus to the Mystery's Opacity creating a quantum state of always on &amp; always off. However, this was not the design of magic to have it check its own Withstand. Because there is a Matter spell that has Durability as a Withstand and it increased Durability.<br /> <br /> There were also examples of lowering Resolve/Composure through Mental Spells and thus creating a chain effect that would reduce someone's Resolve/Composure down to 1, but again this is circular logic that was not intended, only if the Withstand changes outside the spell's mechanics do you re-evaluate Withstand. You can also use another spell to increase the Withstand against a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was part of that argument and no firm comment either way was agreed on. DaveB has said that a spell checks its withstand rating all the time. Its why if you use willpower to increase a reistantance trait that is a spells withstabnd you can temp stop having a spell work on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:07:46-08:00","id":1172872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was part of that argument and no firm comment either way was agreed on. </div> </div> </div>Hm, interesting, it seems that was the design because that would be the only way it works. Besides, why would a spell check its own Withstand? Sounds pretty silly to me honestly, and again would result in what I described above, so its pretty much a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:10:09-08:00","id":1172874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172869#post1172869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s to cast the spell in the first place, reducing Opacity via Scrutiny doesn\u2019t deal with Withstand at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the withstand rating changes during a spells duration then it gets reevaluated. So the Path spell now has the same potency as the withdstand rating of the mystery its on and therefore is suppressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:12:17-08:00","id":1172875,"title":"","content":"Then reapplies... once it rechecks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:12:33-08:00","id":1172876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172872#post1172872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, interesting, it seems that was the design because that would be the only way it works. Besides, why would a spell check its own Withstand? Sounds pretty silly to me honestly, and again would result in what I described above, so its pretty much a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell checks its withstand rating vs the target continually. I originally argued that it only checked withstand when first cast but DaveB said it worked continually has there hasnt been any discussion about how all the other spells like shaping etc therefore work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:13:52-08:00","id":1172877,"title":"","content":"It is checking the target's withstand aside from the spell, seems pretty simple to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:14:19-08:00","id":1172878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172875#post1172875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then reapplies... once it rechecks.</div> </div> </div> </div> It wont though, If the original opacity is 3, your path spell has potency 4 then the withstand is 3, your spell ends up with potency 1 which raises the opacity to 4, the spell rechecks and now has zero potency so is suppressed. Thats it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:14:20-08:00","id":1172879,"title":"","content":"Arguing that a spell checks it\u2019s Withstand against itself led to debuffs that reinforced themselves beyond the actual, deliberate attempts of the Mage casting the spell. Spells don\u2019t seem to be intended to be self-reinforcing though as that would be closer to the Practice of Dynamics than it would be to any one fvthe example spells in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:15:09-08:00","id":1172880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172879#post1172879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing that a spell checks it\u2019s Withstand against itself led to debuffs that reinforced themselves beyond the actual, deliberate attempts of the Mage casting the spell. Spells don\u2019t seem to be intended to be self-reinforcing though as that would be closer to the Practice of Dynamics than it would be to any one fvthe example spells in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not checking vs itself. Its checking vs the NEW opacity of the mystery that you have just raised via the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:16:17-08:00","id":1172883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172874#post1172874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the withstand rating changes during a spells duration then it gets reevaluated. So the Path spell now has the same potency as the withdstand rating of the mystery its on and therefore is suppressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would seem to suggest that <br /> @Talsorblackfire is correct, and that your interpretation isn\u2019t as it would be stupid to create a spell that renders itself useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:17:29-08:00","id":1172885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172879#post1172879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing that a spell checks it\u2019s Withstand against itself led to debuffs that reinforced themselves beyond the actual, deliberate attempts of the Mage casting the spell. Spells don\u2019t seem to be intended to be self-reinforcing though as that would be closer to the Practice of Dynamics than it would be to any one fvthe example spells in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a sleep spell with potency 3 vs somebody with a resolve of 2. The spell works on that person, now if somehow they were able to spend willpower to raise their resolve to 4 the spell would not work on them (for that turn) according to Dave saying that a spell continually checks the withstand rating of its target. When the withstand changes the spell gets reevaulated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:17:32-08:00","id":1172886,"title":"","content":"So it is clear that you don't really understand what we are discussing here.<br /> <br /> If a spell does something to a target, it does not re-assess the Withstand based on the modification based on the spell. It is that simple. It checks the base Withstand or the Withstand outside of the spell's effect.<br /> <br /> I mean if you want to make the argument that it checks against the thing the spell modifies then yeah, most spells don't work. Again, that is obviously not the intent.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> A door is boosted by a spell with Matter to have a durability of 4 (Potency 4, Durability 3, 1 Potency effects the door). The Potency is never lost, because 0 Potency spells can take effect when Withstand is lowered, you are mistaken in thinking the spell actually loses Potency. The Spell is still a Potency 4 Spell, it just boosted the door with the 1 Potency it had over the Withstand. It is still a 4 Potency Spell, Potency is never lost until the spell ends because that is how a spell that was initially Withstood (3 Potency vs 3 Composure) can take effect when the target's Composure drops to 2 or 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added example 01-03-2018, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:19:33-08:00","id":1172887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172886#post1172886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is clear that you don't really understand what we are discussing here.<br /> <br /> If a spell does something to a target, it does not re-assess the Withstand based on the modification based on the spell. It is that simple. It checks the base Withstand or the Withstand outside of the spell's effect.<br /> <br /> I mean if you want to make the argument that it checks against the thing the spell modifies then yeah, most spells don't work. Again, that is obviously not the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no mention of base withstand in any of the text, there wasnt also any mention of spells reevaluating withstand ratings if they change either, but whatever.<br /> <br /> It only breaks a very few spells, such as shaping, honing the form, any that manipulate the same stat they use for a withstand rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-03-2018, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:25:06-08:00","id":1172893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172886#post1172886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is clear that you don't really understand what we are discussing here.<br /> <br /> If a spell does something to a target, it does not re-assess the Withstand based on the modification based on the spell. It is that simple. It checks the base Withstand or the Withstand outside of the spell's effect.<br /> <br /> I mean if you want to make the argument that it checks against the thing the spell modifies then yeah, most spells don't work. Again, that is obviously not the intent.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> A door is boosted by a spell with Matter to have a durability of 4 (Potency 4, Durability 3, 1 Potency effects the door). The Potency is never lost, because 0 Potency spells can take effect when Withstand is lowered, you are mistaken in thinking the spell actually loses Potency. The Spell is still a Potency 4 Spell, it just boosted the door with the 1 Potency it had over the Withstand. It is still a 4 Potency Spell, Potency is never lost until the spell ends because that is how a spell that was initially Withstood (3 Potency vs 3 Composure) can take effect when the target's Composure drops to 2 or 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never said potency gets lost. If a door has durability 3, its withstand is 3, if you raise its durability to 4 its withstand becomes 4. Potency 4 vs withstand now 4= no spell which means back to withstand 3 which means spell on, spell off, spell on, spell of stuff<br /> <br /> Its even worse if you want to lower somebodys stat. You only need potency 6 to lower somebody with stamina 5 to 1 via degrading the form. If the withstand gets reevaluated everytime withstand changes, go work it out. I did awhile ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-03-2018, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:28:16-08:00","id":1172896,"title":"","content":"It seems weird to me that a spell might invalidate itself. It also means more bang for your buck with lower Potency debuff spells. In the end though this comes down to the same argument as a moving AoE spell, nothing in the text explicitly precludes it one way or the other. So just maintain consistency at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-03-2018, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:28:45-08:00","id":1172897,"title":"","content":"I think you should check over my example as well, but I mean it is pretty clear that was the intent because again those spells will not work otherwise.<br /> <br /> This spell is also extremely wicked because each time you lower Opacity through Scrutiny it remains at the Potency of the spell, which if magic works based on my assumption means you better remove the spell if you want to achieve any type of answers. Which also means you could either be conniving by having a low Potency spell to provide lots of false info, or you can have a powerful potent spell with lots of incorrect info that gives you a small chance of revelation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:38:20-08:00","id":1172900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172897#post1172897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should check over my example as well, but I mean it is pretty clear that was the intent because again those spells will not work otherwise.<br /> <br /> This spell is also extremely wicked because each time you lower Opacity through Scrutiny it remains at the Potency of the spell, which if magic works based on my assumption means you better remove the spell if you want to achieve any type of answers. Which also means you could either be conniving by having a low Potency spell to provide lots of false info, or you can have a powerful potent spell with lots of incorrect info that gives you a small chance of revelation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry you lost me. Im not sure what your example is trying to show. Im well aware the spell is still potency 4 but only has X effect because of withstand. If the withstand rating gets continually checked by a spell (which dave says it does) then ANY time the withstand rating equals the potency of the spell then that spell no longer has an effect, by no longer having an effect it stops the change in the withstand rating in the first place so it has an effect again which causes it to no longer have an effect, on and on and on.<br /> <br /> We then get to the strange case of stamina 5 vs potency 6 degrade spell, the spell beats the withstand of 5 by 1 meaning that 1 potency is left to reduce stamina to 4. Withstand gets rechecked and its now 4 so 2 potency is now left to reduce stamina to 3, which means 3 is left to reduce to 2 then 1.<br /> <br /> This only happens if withstand gets continually checked. Personally i thought and continue to rule its only checked when the spell is cast. Solves all this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:45:42-08:00","id":1172908,"title":"","content":"However you want to roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T06:39:08-08:00","id":1172981,"title":"","content":"TL;DR- ignore a spell's own effects on the trait that Withstands it when determining how much it's Withstood, lest silly cyclical shenanigans occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T06:56:34-08:00","id":1172986,"title":"","content":"Makes just as much sense as only checking Withstand once, and fits RAI and RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T07:27:02-08:00","id":1172993,"title":"","content":"However, one question this does bring up is how does spell on spell stacking work in regards to Focused Mage Sight? Do you analyze the most recent spell? Do you analyze the highest opacity first? My gut feeling is you analyze the highest opacity first then work your way through layers making it possible to hide false information with a weaker spell under a more powerful spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T07:43:43-08:00","id":1172997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172986#post1172986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes just as much sense as only checking Withstand once, and fits RAI and RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it has definitely been clarified that temporarily raising a resistance attribute, whether with WP or other means can and will raise withstand and temporarily void the effect of a spell temporarily.<br /> <br /> Eg, Psychic Domination with Potency 4 vs someone with Resolve 3. If they spend willpower to buff it to 5 for a turn, or if someone puts a scene long Resolve+2 buff on them, they are no longer affected by the spell until the temporary buff goes away.<br /> <br /> I had a pretty violent reaction to learning this the first time because I believe it leads to absolutely stupid counter-intuitive situations, but this has, in fact, been confirmed. I'll see if I can find the last discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T07:55:59-08:00","id":1172999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172997#post1172997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it has definitely been clarified that temporarily raising a resistance attribute, whether with WP or other means can and will raise withstand and temporarily void the effect of a spell temporarily.<br /> <br /> Eg, Psychic Domination with Potency 4 vs someone with Resolve 3. If they spend willpower to buff it to 5 for a turn, or if someone puts a scene long Resolve+2 buff on them, they are no longer affected by the spell until the temporary buff goes away.<br /> <br /> I had a pretty violent reaction to learning this the first time because I believe it leads to absolutely stupid counter-intuitive situations, but this has, in fact, been confirmed. I'll see if I can find the last discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, obviously if you temporarily raise Withstand it can null a spell. That isn\u2019t what\u2019s being contested. What\u2019s in question is whether a spell can do that to itself. My answer is no because it leads to a situation where spells null themselves or cycle Withstand down to 0 which I think is nonsense. Totalgit is saying the fix is to only check Withstand once, which obviously isn\u2019t what\u2019s intended in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T08:19:00-08:00","id":1173006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172797-path-to-jerusalem-cow?p=1172999#post1172999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, obviously if you temporarily raise Withstand it can null a spell. That isn\u2019t what\u2019s being contested. What\u2019s in question is whether a spell can do that to itself. My answer is no because it leads to a situation where spells null themselves or cycle Withstand down to 0 which I think is nonsense. Totalgit is saying the fix is to only check Withstand once, which obviously isn\u2019t what\u2019s intended in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, I misunderstood the contention.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I would have no problems houseruling that a spell can't consider any modifications it makes to its own Withstanding trait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T08:58:16-08:00","id":1173010,"title":"","content":"So, if we base spell stacking on the highest Opacity being the first to be scrutinized when using Focused Mage Sight (FMS for short) then I suppose the next question becomes, what information do you gleam from something being analyzed with FMS.<br /> <br /> Example: Let's say you use Corpse Mask to mask the death of someone by magic to appear they were burned to death instead of electrocuted (Firebolt vs. Thunderbolt). Corpse Mask has a Potency of 1 and provokes a Clash of Will on Death Mage Sight being used. The Thunderbolt/Firebolt obviously had a high Potency, so the spell is being analyzed with Forces and they determine that the subject died from immolation based on their FMS findings and go off to find that fireball slinging mage that happens to have a rote in that spell.<br /> <br /> Would this be accurate? In a way, Path to Jerusalem can be used in minor ways from other arcana, but limited in scope. Also, my suspicion is that once you tear an Opacity of a spell down to less than another spell then it suddenly vanishes and you suddenly notice there is something else hidden. Let me know what you think and how you analyze spell stacking with FMS.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T09:05:14-08:00","id":1173012,"title":"","content":"I may be having a dense moment, but I don\u2019t understand the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T10:09:19-08:00","id":1173027,"title":"","content":"I was just making sure I understood how spell stacking worked in regards to FMS. Because it would be possible to hide a spell under another spell hidden under another spell.<br /> <br /> Basically, is it a layer cake scenario where the last spell cast is on top? Or is it a density question from a top-down-view of a glass, you basically only see the portion with the highest density (Opacity). Because you can't analyze 3 different spells at the same time, at least there is no mechanic that handles that or how that would work at present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-03-2018, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T10:46:05-08:00","id":1173041,"title":"","content":"I presume it\u2019s like a cake, Path to Jerusalem goes into effect complicating Scrutiny (False Nimbus signature) before the Corpse Mask it was cast on gets its turn at complicating Scrutiny (Killed by fire not lightning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T04:47:18-08:00","id":1173194,"title":"","content":"Where was the spoiler with this spell posted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T04:59:03-08:00","id":1173195,"title":"","content":"It was part of the Google Document shared by Dave in this development news: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for-miles-and-miles-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for...the-awakening/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}